U.S. Treasury Bonds

U.S. Treasury Bonds are issued by the U.S. government and are considered a low-risk investment.

Expected return: Approximately 4.5% per year.

Investment period: 5 years.

Risks: Rising interest rates can reduce their market value if sold before maturity. Inflation can reduce purchasing power.

Key advantage: Predictable returns and relatively high capital stability when held to maturity.
